input combined) \"\"]\n   934\t      (let [state' (assoc state :pending-input nil)\n   935\t            parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n   936\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   937\t                                  :clj Exception\n   938\t                                  :cljs js/Error) error\n   939\t                          {:error error}))]\n   940\t        (eval-parsed state' combined parsed)))))\n   941\t\n   942\t\n   943\t(defn repl-state\n   944\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n   945\t\n   946\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n   947\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n   948\t   operation.\n   949\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n   950\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n   951\t   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n   952\t   further evaluation.  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n   953\t   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).\"\n   954\t  [state]\n   955\t  {:lang (:lang state)\n   956\t   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n   957\t                 (map (fn [[sym [root _]]] [sym root]))\n   958\t                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n   959\t   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n   960\t        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n   961\t        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n   962\t        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n   963\t                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n   964\t                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n   965\t   :running? (:running? state)\n   966\t   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n   967\t            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n   968\t   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n   969\t   :remote {:connected? false}